                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Is AR makeup try-on necessary for a beauty app in 2026?</h3>
                                        <p>For colour cosmetics (lipstick, foundation, eyeshadow), yes — it's expected. For skincare, no — routine builders and skin analysis matter more.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the ROI of subscription in beauty apps?</h3>
                                        <p>Subscription lifts blended LTV 2-4x for beauty. A 25-35% subscription attach rate is achievable and shifts unit economics dramatically.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I use Perfect Corp or build custom AR?</h3>
                                        <p>Perfect Corp for most brands — proven SDK, faster to market. Build custom only if you have >50 SKUs across multiple categories and need deep customization. Custom AR takes 10-16 weeks and $40K-150K.</p>
                                        <h3>How do I handle multi-shade complexity in the app?</h3>
                                        <p>Ship an AI shade-match onboarding as the first-run experience. Save shade profile per user. Show 'perfect match' → 'close alternatives' → 'try on' flow. This lifts CVR 20-40% versus a generic shade picker.</p>
